WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.485 --> 00:00:01.356
- Good morning believe nation.

00:00:01.356 --> 00:00:03.190
Today's message is...

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:06.197
- Keep going. Over to you, John Legend.

00:00:06.197 --> 00:00:08.368
(rooster crows)

00:00:08.368 --> 00:00:11.352
♫ I wake up every morning,

00:00:11.352 --> 00:00:13.848
♫ Espresso keep me going,

00:00:13.848 --> 00:00:17.331
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:00:17.331 --> 00:00:19.614
- The thing is every
successful person you know

00:00:19.614 --> 00:00:23.114
has failed at what they love to do before.

00:00:24.421 --> 00:00:27.556
I've been unsuccessful in my career.

00:00:27.556 --> 00:00:28.833
You just didn't know about it

00:00:28.833 --> 00:00:29.866
because I wasn't famous yet

00:00:29.866 --> 00:00:31.317
and I was trying to be famous.

00:00:31.317 --> 00:00:34.150
I was trying to get a
record deal for six years

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:36.611
and I kept getting turned down

00:00:36.611 --> 00:00:38.759
and any successful person you know

00:00:38.759 --> 00:00:41.232
even though is seems like
everything just happened for them

00:00:41.232 --> 00:00:43.798
it usually was preceded
by a bunch of failure

00:00:43.798 --> 00:00:45.957
or at least a significant amount

00:00:45.957 --> 00:00:49.092
but the great ones aren't
the ones that don't fail.

00:00:49.092 --> 00:00:50.868
They're the ones that
learn from their failure

00:00:50.868 --> 00:00:52.424
and they keep going and they're persistent

00:00:52.424 --> 00:00:54.444
and they're tenacious and for me,

00:00:54.444 --> 00:00:58.611
I was trying to get a
record deal from '98 to 2004

00:01:01.283 --> 00:01:04.185
and I got turned down by
every major record label

00:01:04.185 --> 00:01:06.519
including the one I'm signed to now

00:01:06.519 --> 00:01:10.780
and for me that means
that even when you hear no

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:12.103
you have to keep going
through all those nos

00:01:12.103 --> 00:01:12.954
until you get to a yes.

00:01:12.954 --> 00:01:14.692
- So what do you think?

00:01:14.692 --> 00:01:16.852
- For me, usually if I start a project

00:01:16.852 --> 00:01:19.847
it doesn't matter how
hard it is or it will be

00:01:19.847 --> 00:01:23.040
I will always continue to finish it.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.826
Like for when I just
started my YouTube channel

00:01:25.826 --> 00:01:27.243
I did the ten day challenge

00:01:27.243 --> 00:01:29.704
and so many things break down.

00:01:29.704 --> 00:01:32.142
The software shut down on me a few times

00:01:32.142 --> 00:01:35.311
but I still stayed up
late and then kept going,

00:01:35.311 --> 00:01:37.494
finish my editing.

00:01:37.494 --> 00:01:40.931
Yeah it was tough that ten days.

00:01:40.931 --> 00:01:43.438
- Benita kept going. She kept going.

00:01:43.438 --> 00:01:44.901
I think people give up too easily.

00:01:44.901 --> 00:01:46.503
I think people quit too soon.

00:01:46.503 --> 00:01:48.884
I look at my YouTube channels,
since we're talking YouTube.

00:01:48.884 --> 00:01:52.217
I started it in 2008 and it wasn't until

00:01:55.223 --> 00:01:58.392
it wasn't until 2014 that I
had my major breakthrough.

00:01:58.392 --> 00:01:59.971
So what is that? Six years.

00:01:59.971 --> 00:02:00.804
Six years.

00:02:01.643 --> 00:02:04.336
Yeah 2014 is when I had
my first kind of big video

00:02:04.336 --> 00:02:05.169
that took off.

00:02:05.169 --> 00:02:06.002
Six years.

00:02:06.002 --> 00:02:08.028
Would you keep at something for six years

00:02:08.028 --> 00:02:11.523
and not see any major results
and just keep doing it?

00:02:11.523 --> 00:02:14.008
I think people just expect instant results

00:02:14.008 --> 00:02:15.401
and when they don't get it they quit

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:16.875
and try to move on to something else

00:02:16.875 --> 00:02:18.106
and then just move on to something else

00:02:18.106 --> 00:02:20.033
and never stick with anything.

00:02:20.033 --> 00:02:21.438
It's the key to success.

00:02:21.438 --> 00:02:22.843
I look at successful companies.

00:02:22.843 --> 00:02:26.059
Look at Harley Davidson, I may
get the numbers a little off

00:02:26.059 --> 00:02:28.566
but they started I think in 1903

00:02:28.566 --> 00:02:31.144
and they made five bikes
that year, five motorcycles.

00:02:31.144 --> 00:02:33.396
In 1904 they made another five motorcycles

00:02:33.396 --> 00:02:35.707
and then the next year they
made like seven motorcycles

00:02:35.707 --> 00:02:38.249
and then two years later they
finally opened up the factory

00:02:38.249 --> 00:02:39.549
and they made 50 motorcycles.

00:02:39.549 --> 00:02:42.475
Like how long would you be
willing to make five motorcycles

00:02:42.475 --> 00:02:45.436
and five motorcycles
and five and then seven?

00:02:45.436 --> 00:02:47.642
Most people think that's a
failure and they quit too soon.

00:02:47.642 --> 00:02:50.637
And so I think with
any goal that you have,

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:52.239
in entrepreneurship or in life,

00:02:52.239 --> 00:02:53.261
you have to keep going.

00:02:53.261 --> 00:02:55.142
Its going to be way harder
than you thought it was,

00:02:55.142 --> 00:02:56.001
it's why it's so important

00:02:56.001 --> 00:02:57.766
that you have a deep passion for it

00:02:57.766 --> 00:02:58.868
because you're going to quit.

00:02:58.868 --> 00:03:00.598
If you're in it just
for some instant result,

00:03:00.598 --> 00:03:03.420
instant money, instant
gratification, you're going to quit

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:05.591
because it's going to
get way way way too hard

00:03:05.591 --> 00:03:09.271
but if you have the deep passion
for it and you keep going

00:03:09.271 --> 00:03:11.848
the prize will be yours.

00:03:11.848 --> 00:03:14.182
So the question of the day today is...

00:03:14.182 --> 00:03:16.597
- What is the thing that you're working on

00:03:16.597 --> 00:03:18.118
that you have been
working on for a long time

00:03:18.118 --> 00:03:19.917
and you still go into?

00:03:19.917 --> 00:03:20.750
- I love it.

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:21.583
- Finish it.

00:03:21.583 --> 00:03:22.483
- Oh I cut you off. I like it.

00:03:22.483 --> 00:03:23.733
You kept going.

00:03:25.533 --> 00:03:26.663
Leave it in the comments below.

00:03:26.663 --> 00:03:28.636
We will join in the discussion.

00:03:28.636 --> 00:03:31.179
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Cristina Archer.

00:03:31.179 --> 00:03:33.373
Cristina thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:03:33.373 --> 00:03:35.823
Your One Word, I really
really really appreciate it

00:03:35.823 --> 00:03:37.553
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:03:37.553 --> 00:03:39.318
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:42.847
I believe in you, I hope you
continue to believe in yourself

00:03:42.847 --> 00:03:43.753
and whatever...

00:03:43.753 --> 00:03:46.109
But your one word is we'll see you soon.

00:03:46.109 --> 00:03:49.883
- No, no much love and we'll
see you again tomorrow morning

00:03:49.883 --> 00:03:50.716
for another...

00:03:50.716 --> 00:03:52.299
- Shot of Espresso.

00:03:53.557 --> 00:03:56.297
♫ I wake up every morning,

00:03:56.297 --> 00:03:59.797
♫ Espresso keep me going.

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:04.939
- In today's world you can't sleep.

00:04:04.939 --> 00:04:06.305
There's no days off,

00:04:06.305 --> 00:04:08.603
there's no time to rest and just kick it

00:04:08.603 --> 00:04:10.299
so you just keep going you know?

00:04:10.299 --> 00:04:12.295
So even though the album just came out

00:04:12.295 --> 00:04:14.606
like they got me in the studio tonight.

00:04:14.606 --> 00:04:16.951
I was in the studio last
night until six a.m.

00:04:16.951 --> 00:04:19.157
We got a full day of like interviews

00:04:19.157 --> 00:04:20.271
and running around in New York

00:04:20.271 --> 00:04:21.665
and then we got studio all night.

00:04:21.665 --> 00:04:22.965
You just keep going.

00:04:22.965 --> 00:04:25.647
And that's how you keep your chops up.

00:04:25.647 --> 00:04:27.911
- There were times in
the last five, six years

00:04:27.911 --> 00:04:29.513
that I was very tempted to just say,

00:04:29.513 --> 00:04:31.525
"You know what? Forget it.

00:04:31.525 --> 00:04:33.675
This is too difficult,
you're not going to come up

00:04:33.675 --> 00:04:35.834
with the album that you need

00:04:35.834 --> 00:04:38.760
and you're driving
yourself crazy with it."

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:42.046
And I was- and of course on top of that,

00:04:42.046 --> 00:04:44.797
I was getting quite a
kicking from the press.

00:04:44.797 --> 00:04:47.047
So at that point in my life

00:04:47.955 --> 00:04:50.705
with so much going on emotionally

00:04:52.239 --> 00:04:54.712
being kicked about by the media

00:04:54.712 --> 00:04:56.024
and the press and the industry

00:04:56.024 --> 00:04:59.191
almost wishing that my career was over

00:05:01.202 --> 00:05:03.702
I was almost ready to give up.

00:05:06.067 --> 00:05:07.390
But part of my motivation,

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:09.968
a very strong part of my
motivation to keep going

00:05:09.968 --> 00:05:12.731
was that I always knew
how terrible it would look

00:05:12.731 --> 00:05:16.794
to young gay kids that were
worried about coming out.

00:05:16.794 --> 00:05:19.975
Not that they necessarily
see a great parallel

00:05:19.975 --> 00:05:23.575
with someone who was
outed when they were 35

00:05:23.575 --> 00:05:26.742
but I think it would be a horrible way

00:05:29.147 --> 00:05:31.481
to leave my career, to
leave people thinking

00:05:31.481 --> 00:05:35.475
that my sexuality took away my marking

00:05:35.475 --> 00:05:37.599
because I just knew that wasn't true

00:05:37.599 --> 00:05:41.198
and I felt a kind of
responsibility not only to myself

00:05:41.198 --> 00:05:44.115
but to young gay people to say look

00:05:45.146 --> 00:05:46.794
because I would feel absolutely sure

00:05:46.794 --> 00:05:48.397
that my marker hadn't left me

00:05:48.397 --> 00:05:50.939
so I felt it really important to say,

00:05:50.939 --> 00:05:54.689
"Look it is not damaging
if you have ability,

00:05:55.537 --> 00:05:59.704
it is not damaging to have
the confidence to come out

00:06:00.982 --> 00:06:03.315
and that in certain parts of life

00:06:03.315 --> 00:06:04.627
it really doesn't matter anymore,

00:06:04.627 --> 00:06:07.553
in certain careers it really
doesn't matter anymore."

00:06:07.553 --> 00:06:10.096
And I think just the success
of the record this time around

00:06:10.096 --> 00:06:12.685
and I hope its continued success

00:06:12.685 --> 00:06:16.018
will alleviate that perception you know?

